Z||000009||cowans||07-06-2001||01:32 PM||||Hi Julian, I have a V8 F40 replica that I just licensed 3 weeks ago. It is still registered as a 86 Fiero but added "Rebodied" to the Registration. You have to go to a Notary/city hall admin with a statement... "to Whom It May Concern" that your Fiero is now a "Rebodied Fiero". Have them 'stamp it' and make sure that your Safety Certificate states the same, then present the documents to the License Bureau. You will now recieve a Registration stating ***198- Fiero Rebodied***. As for the insurance, you will need a certificate stating the value of your car from an authorized appraiser, should be easy in Toronto... I'm in Ottawa.<BR>Sandy||||reg||14
